From 785b426cf918f26b542f5beaee0ea1b3d08f8757 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weidong Sun <sunweidong@linux.alibaba.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 15:25:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] node: publish volume metadata atomically and recover after
 restart

Return cloud device identity in controller responses so NodePublish can
resume without NodeStage after plugin restart. Keep target ownership and
mount properties consistent on republish, publish metadata with rename,
and remove only empty kubelet targets during unpublish.

Accept existing upstream metadata without version, mode or readonly labels.
Use its cloud-volume-id to verify ownership and the current target's Pod
identity when replaying older records. Bound reads and preserve existing
metadata when publication or cleanup fails.

Co-authored-by: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
